          "text": "The pattern indexes as a **primitive monoclinic** cell. The strongest diagnostic sequences are:\n\n- \\(100,300\\): 10.96\u00b0, 33.28\u00b0\n- \\(002,004,006\\): 13.20\u00b0, 26.56\u00b0, 40.34\u00b0\n- \\(010,020,030\\): 14.72\u00b0, 29.68\u00b0, 45.19\u00b0\n- \\(102,204\\): 20.10\u00b0, 40.89\u00b0\n\nA consistent cell is \\(a\\approx8.682\\), \\(b\\approx6.012\\), \\(c\\approx14.428\\) \u00c5, \\(\\beta\\approx111.72^\\circ\\), \\(V\\approx699.7\\) \u00c5\u00b3, with \\(Z=4\\). The observed absence of isolated odd-\\(l\\) \\(h0l\\) reflections supports **P2/c (No. 13, unique axis b)**.\n\nThe lattice and space-group assignment are substantially more secure than the powder-derived atomic coordinates. The coordinates below are a chemically constrained starting model and should receive a final Rietveld refinement before publication.\n\n```cif\ndata_RbHgSbTe3\n_audit_creation_method\n'Powder indexing and chemically constrained direct-space model'\n_chemical_name_common                  'rubidium mercury antimony telluride'\n_chemical_formula_sum                  'Rb Hg Sb Te3'\n_chemical_formula_structural           'RbHgSbTe3'\n_chemical_formula_weight               790.62\n\n_cell_length_a                         8.682(4)\n_cell_length_b                         6.0124(18)\n_cell_length_c                         14.428(6)\n_cell_angle_alpha                      90\n_cell_angle_beta                       111.72(3)\n_cell_angle_gamma                      90\n_cell_volume                           699.7(6)\n_cell_formula_units_Z                  4\n\n_exptl_crystal_density_diffrn          7.51\n\n_space_group_crystal_system            monoclinic\n_space_group_name_H-M_alt              'P 1 2/c 1'\n_space_group_name_Hall                 '-P 2yc'\n_space_group_IT_number                 13\n\n_diffrn_radiation_type                 'Cu Kalpha1'\n_diffrn_radiation_wavelength           1.5406\n\nloop_\n_space_group_symop_id\n_space_group_symop_operation_xyz\n1  'x,y,z'\n2  '-x,y,-z+1/2'\n3  '-x,-y,-z'\n4  'x,-y,z+1/2'\n\nloop_\n_atom_type_symbol\n_atom_type_oxidation_number\nRb  1\nHg  2\nSb  3\nTe -2\n\nloop_\n_atom_site_label\n_atom_site_type_symbol\n_atom_site_symmetry_multiplicity\n_atom_site_Wyckoff_symbol\n_atom_site_fract_x\n_atom_site_fract_y\n_atom_site_fract_z\n_atom_site_occupancy\n_atom_site_U_iso_or_equiv\nRb1 Rb 4 g 0.0418 0.2496 0.1215 1.0 0.025\nHg1 Hg 4 g 0.3372 0.2521 0.3314 1.0 0.018\nSb1 Sb 4 g 0.0054 0.2478 0.3408 1.0 0.018\nTe1 Te 4 g 0.1986 0.6200 0.3381 1.0 0.020\nTe2 Te 4 g 0.6758 0.1975 0.5008 1.0 0.020\nTe3 Te 4 g 0.2587 0.1498 0.1399 1.0 0.020\n```\n\nNo comparably convincing alternative Bravais lattice survived the harmonic-reflection and systematic-absence checks.",
